# Static assets are served verbatim
apps/*/static/

# The Alignment round-trip fixtures, where the **bytes are the assertion** (ADR-0010).
#
# These are frozen Georeference Annotations, and `georeference-annotation.test.ts` requires
# `serialiseAlignment` to reproduce them byte for byte — which is what makes them catch a pre-1.0
# `@allmaps/*` bump that starts writing the document differently. Prettier reflows nested JSON
# arrays onto fewer lines, so formatting them would break that test and, worse, would quietly
# invalidate the one guard standing between an Allmaps upgrade and every Alignment in the field
# being subtly misplaced. Same principle as the served assets above: verbatim or not at all.
packages/core/src/alignment/fixtures/

# Prose. The specification, the ticket ledger, the ADRs, and the contributor documents are
# written and reviewed by hand, and this project has a lot of them. Letting prettier reflow
# their paragraphs and pad their tables turns every later edit into an unreadable diff, and
# markdown is where the reasoning lives here rather than an afterthought. Prettier formats
# code; prose is reviewed by reading it.
*.md
